model leg_on_move
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.2 G1 S-6 (#211, plan §4): a leg has no day of its own, so a move's leg that states an on is refused by the grammar (LOAD-PARSE at the leg's line, choice C-1 (a)). Its twin leg_on_move_twin.tally writes the smaller form: a second move keyed by the first, dated from its day."

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input d0: date
input lag: int

move pay: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt on add_days(d0, lag)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d0 = 2026-03-10 "s"
  lag = 2 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-10), bal(konto, 2026-03-12)
